Maintenance operations for managing scheduled updates to your Database Instance.

USAGE:
  scw mongodb maintenance <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  apply       Apply a maintenance of a MongoDB® Database Instance.
  get         Get a maintenance of a MongoDB® Database Instance.
  list        List all the maintenances of a MongoDB® Database Instance.

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for maintenance
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw mongodb maintenance [command] --help" for more information about a command.
